    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p41-q18-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $y=e^x-e^{-x}$ is an odd function.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(-x)=-f(x)$, so $f$ is odd.",
          "worked": "Let $f(x)=e^x-e^{-x}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=e^{-x}-e^x\\\\&=-(e^x-e^{-x})\\\\&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p41-q18-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence write down the value of $\\displaystyle\\int_{-3}^{3}(e^x-e^{-x})\\,dx$ without finding a primitive.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "The integrand is odd and the limits are symmetric about zero, so\n$$\\int_{-3}^{3}(e^x-e^{-x})\\,dx=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p41-q18-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Explain why the area of this region may be written as $\\displaystyle\\text{area}=2\\int_0^3(e^x-e^{-x})\\,dx$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd symmetry makes the two shaded areas equal; the curve is above the axis for $0<x\\le3$.",
          "worked": "The graph has rotational symmetry about the origin, so the shaded regions have equal unsigned areas. Since $e^x-e^{-x}>0$ for $0<x\\le3$, the integral from $0$ to $3$ gives the right-hand area. Doubling it gives the total area.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p41-q18-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Hence find the area of this region.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2(e^3+e^{-3}-2)\\text{ units}^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=2\\int_0^3(e^x-e^{-x})\\,dx\\\\&=2[e^x+e^{-x}]_0^3\\\\&=2[(e^3+e^{-3})-2]\\\\&=2(e^3+e^{-3}-2)\\text{ units}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ],
    "diagramPlacement": "right-of-prompt"
  },
